-- title:
--   Affine chart with residual transcendence at a supersingular place, q=3
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ denotes `AlgebraicClosure ℚ`, and for a field $K$ a `Place K F` is a valuation subring of $F$ containing the image of $K$, distinct from $F$, whose ring is a principal ideal ring; `ord` is the associated normalised additive valuation and `evalAt f` is the element of $K$ whose image is the residue of $f$ when $f$ is integral at the place, and $0$ otherwise.
--
--   **Fixed data.** A prime $q$ together with the hypothesis $q = 3$; a level $M' \neq 0$ with $q \nmid M'$; a prime $\ell_g$ with $\ell_g \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ and $\ell_g \mid M'$; a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with `A.LiesOverPrime q`, i.e. $q$ is a non-unit of $A$; write $\kappa =$ `ResidueField A`. A finite set $W$ of places of `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'` over $\kappa$ — the latter being the intermediate field of $\kappa((q))$ generated over $\kappa$ by `jqModC κ` and `jqNModC κ M' = qExpand κ M' (jqModC κ)` — with the hypothesis `hW` that membership in $W$ is equivalent to membership in `ssPlaces q M' κ`, that is, to being a place $w$ which is rational (the map $\kappa \to w$'s residue field is surjective), satisfies `IsAffineGeomPlace κ M'`, and has `w.evalAt (jGeomGen κ M') ∈ ssJSet q κ`; and a distinguished element $s \in W$.
--
--   The field `fieldBar q M'` is `xHFunctionFieldBar (q^2 * M') (levelH q M')`, the intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}((q))$ generated over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ by the coefficientwise image of the function field of $X_H$ of level $q^2M'$, where $H =$ `levelH q M'` is the kernel of the reduction map $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/q)^\times$, i.e. the units congruent to $1$ modulo $q$. The field `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` is the intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}((q))$ generated over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ by the coefficientwise images of `modularFunctionFieldFull M'`, the subfield of $\mathbb{Q}((q))$ generated by the expansions `qExpand ℚ d jq` for $d \mid M'$. The hypothesis `hle` is the inclusion `modularFunctionFieldBar M' ≤ fieldBar q M'`.
--
--   Further fixed data: a `ConstantReduction` $R_0$ of $A$ from `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` to `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'`, that is, a valuation subring `R₀.integers` of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` together with a surjective ring homomorphism `R₀.residue` onto `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'` whose kernel is the maximal ideal, a degree-preserving map on places, the requirement that a constant $x$ be integral exactly when $x \in A$, compatibility of residues with $A \to \kappa$, the existence for each nonzero $f$ of a scalar multiple which is integral with nonzero residue, and compatibility of the divisor of an element with that of its residue away from the relevant data. The hypothesis `hR₀` requires that for every Laurent series $y$ with coefficients in $A$ whose coefficientwise image lies in `modularFunctionFieldBar M'`, this image lies in `R₀.integers` and its residue is, as a Laurent series over $\kappa$, the coefficientwise reduction of $y$.
--
--   **Small-constant data.** An intermediate field $k_0$ of $\mathbb{Q}$ in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$; an element $\pi_0 \in k_0$ lying in $A$; with $A_{k_0} :=$ `A.comap (algebraMap k₀ ℚ̄)` the induced valuation subring of $k_0$, the hypotheses that $A_{k_0}$ is a discrete valuation ring, that its maximal ideal is generated by $\pi_0$, that it is a henselian local ring, and that its residue field is algebraically closed; and `hκ`, that every $a \in A$ is congruent modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ to some $c \in k_0$ with $c \in A$.
--
--   **Auxiliary prime and twisting element.** A prime $\ell$ with $\ell \geq 3$, $\ell \neq q$ and $\ell \nmid M'$; an element $\zeta_0 \in k_0$ whose image in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ is a primitive $q\ell$-th root of unity; an element $\varpi_t \in k_0$ lying in $A$ with $\varpi_t^{\,q^2-1} = q\,u$ for some unit $u$ of $A$.
--
--   **Base layer.** An intermediate field $K_b$ of $k_0$ in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $K_b = \bot$; a valuation subring $A_b$ of $K_b$ with $x \in A_b$ iff $x \in A$; a generator $\varpi_b \neq 0$ of the maximal ideal of $A_b$.
--
--   The conclusion is stated for the $k_0$-algebra structure on `fieldBar q M'` obtained by composing $k_0 \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $\overline{\mathbb{Q}} \to$ `fieldBar q M'`. It asserts: for every intermediate field $F_0$ of $k_0$ in `fieldBar q M'` satisfying (LF1)–(LF4) and every valuation subring $W_0$ of $F_0$ satisfying (K2), (K4), (K5-W) and (MODEL), the conjunction (1)–(9) below holds.
--
--   **Hypotheses on $F_0$.** (LF1) an element $f$ of `fieldBar q M'` lies in $F_0$ if and only if every coefficient of $f$, viewed as a Laurent series over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, lies in $k_0$. (LF2) `IntermediateField.adjoin k₀ (Set.range (algebraMap ℚ̄ (fieldBar q M')))` joined with $F_0$ is $\top$. (LF3) for every $\zeta$ in `Idx q` (the primitive $q$-th roots of unity in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$) and every $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$, the automorphism `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` maps $F_0$ into itself; here `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` is the $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-algebra automorphism of `fieldBar q M'` chosen to satisfy `IsLevelAutBar q M' ζ γ` — acting on quotients of integral $q$-expansions of modular forms of level $\Gamma_H(q^2M')$ by the slash action of `conjElem q γ` under any embedding $\iota$ into $\mathbb{C}$ with $\iota\zeta = e^{2\pi i/q}$ — and the identity if no such automorphism exists. (LF4) linear disjointness: for every finite-dimensional intermediate field $K'$ of $k_0$ in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, every $m$, every $c : \mathrm{Fin}\,m \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ and every $a : \mathrm{Fin}\,m \to$ `fieldBar q M'` with all $a_i$ in the join of `IntermediateField.adjoin k₀` of the image of $K'$ with $F_0$, if $c$ is $K'$-linearly independent and $\sum_i c_i a_i = 0$, then $a_i = 0$ for all $i$.
--
--   **Hypotheses on $W_0$.** (K2) for $x \in k_0$: $x \in A$ if and only if the image of $x$ in $F_0$ lies in $W_0$; $W_0$ is a discrete valuation ring; and the image of $\pi_0$ lies in $W_0$ and generates the maximal ideal of $W_0$.
--
--   (K4) for every $g \in$ `modularFunctionFieldFull M'` whose coefficientwise image $\bar g \in$ `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` lies in `R₀.integers`, if for every place $P$ of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ the inequality $0 \le P.\mathrm{ord}(\bar\jmath)$ implies $0 \le P.\mathrm{ord}(\bar g)$, where $\bar\jmath$ is the image of `jq`, and if `R₀.residue` of $\bar g$ lies in the valuation subring of the place $s$, then the image of $\bar g$ in `fieldBar q M'` under `IntermediateField.inclusion hle` lies in $F_0$, the resulting element of $F_0$ lies in $W_0$, and for every $c \in k_0$ lying in $A$ whose residue in $\kappa$ equals $s.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of `R₀.residue` of $\bar g$, the difference of that element and the image of $c$ lies in $W_0$ and in the maximal ideal of $W_0$.
--
--   (K5-W) for every $\zeta$ in `Idx q` and every $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$, and every $f \in F_0$ with `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ f` also in $F_0$: $f \in W_0$ if and only if `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ f` $\in W_0$.
--
--   (MODEL) there exist a subring $B$ of `fieldBar q M'` and an $A_b$-algebra structure `alg` on $B$ such that: (M1) the structure map sends $a \in A_b$ to the image of $a \in K_b \subseteq \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ in `fieldBar q M'`; (M2) $B$ is contained in the join of `IntermediateField.adjoin k₀` of the image of $K_b$ with $F_0$; (M3) every element of that join is of the form $g/h$ with $g, h \in B$, $h \neq 0$; (M4) $B$ is formally smooth over $A_b$; (M5) $B$ is of finite presentation over $A_b$; (M6) $B/\varpi_b B$ has Krull dimension at most $1$; (M7) every element of $B$ lies in $F_0$ and in $W_0$; (M8) the image of $\varpi_b$ is a prime element of $B$; (M9) an element $f$ of $F_0$ lies in $W_0$ exactly when $f h = g$ for some $g, h \in B$ with the image of $\varpi_b$ not dividing $h$; (M10) the image of `jq` in `fieldBar q M'` lies in $B$; (M11) $B$ is stable under `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` for every $\zeta$ in `Idx q` and every $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$; and (M12) for every $\mathbb{F}_{q^2}$-algebra structure on $\kappa$ (with $\mathbb{F}_{q^2} =$ `GaloisField q 2`), every proof that [`DrinfeldCurve.CoordRing q κ`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L21) — the quotient of $\kappa[x_0,x_1]$ by `drinfeldPoly q κ - 1` — is a domain, and every $\zeta$ in `Idx q`, there are a subgroup $C_s$ of the group of $(q+1)$-st roots of unity of $\mathbb{F}_{q^2}$ and a ring homomorphism $\rho$ from $B$ to [`DrinfeldCurve.quotField q κ Cs`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelSemistableCoveringW2.html#L32), the fixed field inside the Drinfeld function field `FractionRing (CoordRing q κ)` of the subgroup generated by the `hFunctionFieldAction` images of the elements $(1,\zeta')$ for $\zeta' \in C_s$, such that: $\mathrm{card}\,C_s = 2\,\cdot$ `placeWidthChar q M' s`, where `placeWidthChar` is `jWidthChar q` of the $j$-value of the place divided by `placeRamificationJ M'` of the place, and `jWidthChar 3 j` is $6$ for $j = 0$ and $1$ otherwise; $\ker\rho$ is the ideal generated by the image of $\varpi_b$; $\rho$ composed with the structure map $A_b \to B$ is reduction $A_b \to \kappa$ followed by $\kappa \to$ `quotField q κ Cs`; every $z$ in `quotField q κ Cs` satisfies $z\,\rho(h) = \rho(g)$ for some $g, h \in B$ with $\rho(h) \neq 0$; an element $z$ of `quotField q κ Cs` lies in the range of $\rho$ precisely when, as an element of the Drinfeld function field, it lies in the image of `CoordRing q κ`; and, for every $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ such that $(\mathrm{redQ}\,q\,\gamma, 1)$ lies in [`DrinfeldCurve.hSubgroup q`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L276) (the kernel of the character $(g,u) \mapsto \det g \cdot u^{q+1}$ on $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{Z}/q) \times \mathbb{F}_{q^2}^\times$), and every $f \in B$ with `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ⁻¹ f` again in $B$, one has $\rho(\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta\,\gamma^{-1}\,f) =$ `hFunctionFieldAction q κ` at that element of `hSubgroup q` applied to $\rho(f)$.
--
--   **Conclusion.** (1) the join of `IntermediateField.adjoin k₀ (Set.range (algebraMap ℚ̄ (fieldBar q M')))` with $F_0$ is $\top$. (2) for $x \in k_0$: $x \in A$ iff the image of $x$ in $F_0$ lies in $W_0$. (3) $W_0$ is a discrete valuation ring. (4) the image of $\pi_0$ lies in $W_0$ and generates its maximal ideal. (5) there exists $t \in W_0$ such that for every polynomial $p$ over $k_0$ all of whose coefficients lie in $A$, if $p$ evaluated at $t$ lies in $W_0$ and in the maximal ideal of $W_0$, then for every index $n$ the image of the coefficient $p_n$ lies in $W_0$ and in the maximal ideal of $W_0$. (6) the clause (K4) above, verbatim. (7) for every $\zeta$ in `Idx q` and every $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$: $F_0$ is stable under `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ`, and for $f \in F_0$ with `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ f` in $F_0$ one has $f \in W_0$ iff its image lies in $W_0$ — that is, (LF3) and (K5-W) combined under a single quantification. (8) the linear disjointness clause (LF4), verbatim. (9) the existence of $(B,\mathrm{alg})$ with all of (M1)–(M12), verbatim as in (MODEL).
--
--   Thus the conclusion reproduces the hypotheses on $F_0$ and $W_0$, with the exception of the coefficient description (LF1), which is not restated, and adds the new conjunct (5): the existence of an element of $W_0$ whose residue is transcendental over the residue field of $A_{k_0}$, in the stated polynomial form.
--
--   This is the functorial form of the affine-chart statement for the semistable model of the modular curve of level $q^2M'$ at a supersingular place in the case $q = 3$, read on given level field $F_0$, valuation ring $W_0$ and chart $B$ over the base layer, and augmented by the residual transcendence of a coordinate; the new conjunct is the content of [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.supersingularDVR_residuallyTranscendental_of_affineChart_of_eq_three_of_dvd`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.supersingularDVR_residuallyTranscendental_of_affineChart_of_eq_three_of_dvd). It is used by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_klevel_supersingularDVR_smoothPointPackages_nodePresentations_nodeCharts_hasseJ_drinfeldInertia_of_eq_three_of_dvd_affineChart`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_klevel_supersingularDVR_smoothPointPackages_nodePresentations_nodeCharts_hasseJ_drinfeldInertia_of_eq_three_of_dvd_affineChart), where the charts at the supersingular points are assembled into the semistable covering, the special fibre being described by the Drinfeld curve $x y^q - x^q y = 1$ and its quotients by subgroups of $\mu_{q+1}$.
